{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk0MjAwMA==","is_bot":false,"login":"magnus919","name":"Magnus Hedemark"},"body":"The A07 quota-success control used the production-default timeout while exercising large frozen provider bodies. Give this fixture an explicit finite 60-second timeout so it can verify quota accounting and ownership transfer independently of default-budget throughput. PubMed still derives its aggregate budget using the unchanged 90% rule (54 seconds in this fixture). Failures now include the case ID and elapsed time.\n\nProduction defaults, deadline calculations, payloads, assertions, and all 17 original resource-test identities remain unchanged. The README states the fixture's scope and makes no production-performance claim. No portal-visible contract changes.\n\nValidation:\n- Formatting passed, the eight-body quota selector passed, and all six context controls passed.\n- Complete A07 gate passed: 301 tests, including every original resource-test identity.\n- Scoped pre-commit passed. The all-files run found an existing unrelated Ruff-format change; its exact before/after was preserved and the file restored to HEAD.\n- AST-only graphify update completed; zero-node warnings were retained. No API calls.\n\nThe gate's native command exited 0. Its initial cleanup check failed because two sanitizer fixtures remained; a separately reviewed, source-bound preservation moved those exact fixtures with inode/content evidence. The original cleanup failure is retained and was not relabeled. Full-workspace, platform and published-head CI remain separate required evidence.\n\nRelated to #936 and #879.\n","headRefOid":"1317e3b9e5e5538075c6e79ef32e807bc3d46270","mergeStateStatus":"CLEAN","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-10-19T23:12:32Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/magnus919/SlopSearX/actions/runs/39340107249/job/118359289292","name":"droid-review","startedAt":"2026-10-19T23:12:39Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowNam